  era: "c. 2600\u20131900 BCE \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Harappan trade
  text: Harappans traded across the region and overseas. Mesopotamian texts mention Meluhha, probably the Indus region. Harappan seals and beads have been found in Mesopotamia and the Gulf, and carnelian, timber, ivory and cotton were likely exports.
